{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "A conjoiner fabrial: a pair of linked reed pens that lets people on Roshar write to each other over long distances.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "28" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "A conjoiner fabrial made by trapping a spren in a ruby and splitting it between two reed pens, so that each pen copies the other's movements and people can write to each other over long distances.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "28" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "100" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "Whoever writes with one reed powers the movement of its twin, so a working spanreed weighs about double what a normal pen does.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Turning the ruby's setting switches between modes: asking the other side to talk, confirming a message came through, and linking the two reeds so they move together. Writers switch back to show they are done.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "28" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "A spanreed is made like other conjoiners, by trapping a spren in a ruby and splitting it in two.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "100" }]
    }
  ],
  "history": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Spread of the spanreed",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "44" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "52" }
              ]
            },
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "39" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "24" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "The Alethi royal family was using spanreeds by 1155, yet in 1168, early in the War of Reckoning, they were still seen as a new invention.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "44" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "52" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "By the war's sixth year they were in common use in the Vorin lands, found in places as far apart as the Shattered Plains, Kharbranth and the remote Davar estates.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "39" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "By 1173 Tashikk was growing into a spanreed hub. People and places kept reeds linked to Tashikki businesses, whose operators could be hired to pass on messages, look things up and make enquiries.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "24" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "mechanics": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Writing by spanreed",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "28" },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "28" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "64" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "100" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "28" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Spanreed desks have to be perfectly level for the reeds to work, and many come with levelling devices built in.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "28" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Vorin men who don't write can still use a spanreed, switching the gem on and off to show they are alive.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "28" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "64" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The farther apart two reeds are, the heavier they become once active, which can be used to work out where the other reed is.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "100" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "28" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Limits",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "88" },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "88" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "5" }
              ]
            },
            { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "20" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "A moving spanreed can't send a clear message to a twin that is standing still.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "88" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Fabrials depend on the user's frame of reference, so two reeds on the same ship work normally, and the planet's motion and curve don't affect them.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "88" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "5" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Spanreeds can't link the Physical and Cognitive Realms.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "20" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Aluminum",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "9" }]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Huio noticed that aluminum affects the spren trapped in a spanreed's ruby: after he tinkered with one, its twin would only move sideways. Rushu built on this to make Rysn's chair float.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "9" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
